==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*Infinite [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 9.33 seconds<sup>280f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Chickful A]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**10 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**6 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**4 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The angel enemies in this stage all push with terrifying ease, while the starred aliens prevent you from pushing back without barrier breakers. You should have all crystals from [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 2 by the time you challenge this stage to make this it feasible, otherwise you're fighting aliens far stronger than they should be at this point; obtaining even more crystals makes the stage even easier.

[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] is a no brainer here, and when adequately boosted can work as your lone meatshield here with the help of research combos such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]]. The UltraBaaBaas in the stage demand barrier breakers, for which [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]] should be enough, though pre-TF is less effective due to its longer foreswing and attack cycle; [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Marine]] may also work if one doesn't own The Kitty of Liberty, sporting similar range and a quick attack rate with a high Barrier Breaker rate. Any ranged DPS units like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cat]] [[Brainwashed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Variants]] or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] can and will kill all of the enemies here eventually. Talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] is also extremely helpful in slowing down Boraphim if your Ramen Cat can't handle him alone.

You can stack units on the UltraBaaBaas at the start of the level, such as Sanzo Cats as well as other ranged attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]].

==Hints==
These hints only appear as defeat messages given after losing the stage.
*Equip units with a low deployment<br>cost and deploying them quickly to<br>slow the enemy's progress.<br>This a fundamental strategy.
*Starred Aliens are tough cookies. If you don't<br>collect all Treasures from Cats of the<br>the Cosmos Ch. 2, there may be no hope.

